ttps://api.github.com/users/thxmike/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thxmike/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thxmike/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thxmike/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thxmike/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/comments/906608095","html_url":"https://github.com/typeorm/typeorm/issues/7516#issuecomment-906608095","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/7516","id":906608095,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAyVBJc42Cb3f","user":{"login":"bartdorsey","id":362049,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MjA0OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/362049?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bartdorsey","html_url":"https://github.com/bartdorsey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bartdorsey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bartdorsey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bartdorsey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bartdorsey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bartdorsey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bartdorsey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bartdorsey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bartdorsey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bartdorsey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-08-26T17:37:08Z","updated_at":"2021-08-26T17:37:08Z","body":"So this is happening because you are trying to output ES modules from the typescript compilation step, and down inside of [`DirectoryExportedClassesLoader.js`](https://github.com/bartdorsey/budgetcal/blob/main/backend/node_modules/typeorm/util/DirectoryExportedClassesLoader.js) It does uses `require()` to dynamically load the modules. \r\n\r\nI'm not sure if there's an easy fix for TypeORM here. If they switch to `await import()` instead of `require()` for the dynamic loading of the entities, then it'll break for everyone NOT using ES modules in Node.\r\n\r\nUnless it could do some introspection and check if require exists, and if it does, use the require function, else use the await import function.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/comments/906608095/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"bartdorsey","id":362049,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MjA0OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/362049?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bartdorsey","html_url":"https://github.com/bartdorsey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bartdorsey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bartdorsey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bartdorsey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bartdorsey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bartdorsey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bartdorsey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bartdorsey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bartdorsey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bartdorsey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/comments/922501289","html_url":"https://github.com/typeorm/typeorm/issues/7516#issuecomment-922501289","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/7516","id":922501289,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAyVBJc42_ECp","user":{"login":"chetrit","id":10844336,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNl